  "prefLabel": "En 1016.02 Notice of Grievance",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1016.02 Notice of Grievance. When a dispute occurs that is not resolved through informal conversation, the party with the grievance shall notify the other party of the dispute in writing with a description of the nature of the dispute and relevant facts, the provisions of this chapter believed to be at issue, and desired outcome. The receiving party shall acknowledge the notification, identify a representative with the authority to resolve the dispute, and commence good faith efforts to resolve the dispute within 10 business days.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
}
